tered unusual journal logging behavior during kernel crash troubleshooting. It was also used as a source system for upgrades and as the target OS after migrating from CentOS 7.6/7.9, though it was noted that Wi-Fi configuration worked correctly in this version. OpenEuler 22.03 is also used in contexts involving MLNX_OFED_LINUX support and driver version reporting during system testing.<SEP>OpenEuler 22.03 is a version of the OpenEuler operating system where xrdp functions normally without black screen issues."}
